profile: tinyrustlm-mirust.constraints.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T20:20:00Z

hard_constraints:
  - Plain PHP site; no WordPress, front-end framework, telemetry, analytics, or remote inference.
  - Project sites receive no prompts or model bytes.
  - One exact six-member SLM2 path; no obsolete format, compatibility, migration, alias, fallback, response repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, or accepted debt.
  - MemoryEndpoints.com has exactly the two separately governed uses in totem.uai and taboo.uai; neither lane silently acts for the other.
  - Redundant prelaunch memory copies stay current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  - Publish only clean pushed manifest-bound source, then prove exact HTTPS bytes and headers.

